to Marrakech. Discover Morocco’s northern and southern highlights — from Tangier and Chefchaouen to the Sahara Desert and Marrakech — blending culture, history, and desert adventure.</p><div class='et-ctas'><a class='et-btn' href='#et-iti'>See the day-by-day plan <svg aria-hidden='true' width='16' height='16'><use href='#et-i-arrow'/></svg></a><a class='et-btn et-btn-w et-btn-wa' href='https://wa.me/212661292596?text=Hello%20Epic%20Travel%20Morocco,%20I%20am%20interested%20in%20the%20Highlights%20of%20Morocco%20(6%20days).%20' target='_blank' rel='noopener'><svg aria-hidden='true'><use href='#et-i-wa'/></svg>Book on WhatsApp</a></div></div></section><div class='et'><div class='et-wrap'><div class='et-facts'><div><b>6 days</b><span>5 nights</span></div><div><b>Tangier</b><span>starting point</span></div><div><b>Marrakech</b><span>end of the tour</span></div><div><b>Private</b><span>your own driver &amp; vehicle</span></div></div></div></div><section class='et et-sec' id='et-iti'><div class='et-wrap et-tour'><div><h3 style='font-size:20px'>Route</h3><div class='et-stops'><span>Tangier</span><span>Chefchaouen</span><span>Volubilis</span><span>Fes</span><span>Ifrane</span><span>Merzouga</span><span>Todra Gorge</span><span>Dades Valley</span><span>Ait Benhaddou</span><span>Marrakech</span></div><div class='et-iti-h'><div><span class='et-eye'>Itinerary</span><h2>Day by day</h2></div><button type='button' class='et-tog' data-o='0'>Open all days</button></div><div class='et-iti'><details class='et-day et-rv' open><summary><span class='et-node'>1</span><small>Day 1</small><b>Tangier · Chefchaouen</b></summary><div class='et-day-b'><p>We will assist you, pick you up at the airport/hotel and drive to see the Hercules Caves, then we continue with an excited feeling to explore more, along the typical Moroccan mountains located in the north of the Rif. The holy town of Chefchaouen breathes an atmosphere of profound serenity with its blue and white charm appearing along the road. Walk around the Kasbah, the Medina, the Jewish quarter, the Berber souks, and the artisan quarters. Later, enjoy the rest of the day in the blue town.</p></div></details><details class='et-day et-rv'><summary><span class='et-node'>2</span><small>Day 2</small><b>Chefchaouen · Volubilis · Fes</b></summary><div class='et-day-b'><p>After breakfast in the Riad, we will have a free morning to enjoy extra time in the blue city. We leave Chefchaouen at noon. Our authentic journey departs toward Volubilis, the famous Roman ruins site in Morocco. We will get in touch with its great history and learn about this archaeological site. Later, we will continue to the historical city of Fes.</p></div></details><details class='et-day et-rv'><summary><span class='et-node'>3</span><small>Day 3</small><b>Fes city tour</b></summary><div class='et-day-b'><p>Your licensed national guide will meet you after breakfast for a fascinating historical tour of the spiritual capital of Morocco, Fes. The city, nestled in the hills, is mystical and magical. You’ll be transported in time as you visit the most beautiful madrassa in the nation, Al Kairaouine. Wander through the ancient medina and souks. Visit the photogenic tannery and learn about the first steps in processing hides into the beautiful leather handicrafts available around you. At the end of the formal tour, return to the riad for a rest or continue to independently discover the city. The rest of the day is free.</p></div></details><details class='et-day et-rv'><summary><span class='et-node'>4</span><small>Day 4</small><b>Fes · Ifrane · Midelt · Erfoud · Merzouga (desert)</b></summary><div class='et-day-b'><p>After breakfast, we hit the road to Ifrane. We stop by the lion symbol that sits in the heart of the town — carved by a German soldier during WWII. During this journey, we experience glimpses of the Atlas Mountains. Stop along the famous cedar forest, the largest in Morocco, where you may see the Barbary apes. Lunch on the spot, then we drive to Merzouga via the Anti-Atlas. Carry on down the road via the magnificent Ziz Gorges carved through limestone mountains, stopping for panoramic views along the way — seeing the dense canopy of palms wedged between ancient striated cliffs which date to the Jurassic period. Then it’s straight to the impressive Erg Chebbi dunes. Later, embark on our camel ride for an hour through the stunning dunes — the clean air and the beautiful sunset will provide us unforgettable moments. We continue to the camp after sunset where you will be welcomed with tea and nuts. Dinner and overnight stay in a luxury camp.</p></div></details><details class='et-day et-rv'><summary><span class='et-node'>5</span><small>Day 5</small><b>Sahara Desert · Toudgha Gorges · Dades Valley</b></summary><div class='et-day-b'><p>Enjoy breakfast in the camp before we start our adventure trip. We will visit the surrounding Berber villages and get closer contact with the Berber culture. We drive to Rissani, an ancient capital for the Alaouite Sultans town. Drive towards Toudgha Gorges. The alluring beauty of the lush palm grove along the valley is known for breathtaking views. Driving the windy and thin road will get our full attention as we get into the Gorges, allowing you to feel the unbelievable glory of the massive canyon walls. We then continue to Dades Valley.</p></div></details><details class='et-day et-rv'><summary><span class='et-node'>6</span><small>Day 6</small><b>Dades Valley · Ouarzazate · Marrakech</b></summary><div class='et-day-b'><p>After breakfast, we drive to Kalaat M’gouna, “the Rose City”. Carry on to Skoura and drive through the “Road of the Thousand Kasbahs” to Ouarzazate city. We stop by The Atlas Studios — the world’s largest film studio by acreage — and continue to Ait Benhaddou. It’s a famous kasbah and the backdrop for many Hollywood hits such as Gladiator, The Mummy, and Alexander. Crossing the dramatic Tizi N’Tichka Pass (2260m), we arrive in Marrakech in the afternoon.</p></div></details></div><div class='et-note'><svg aria-hidden='true'><use href='#et-i-info'/></svg><div><b>Tailor-made:</b> Every itinerary can be adapted — start date, number of days, hotels and stops. Tell us your dates and we send you a detailed quote.</div></div></div><aside class='et-side'><div class='et-book'><div class='et-book-h et-dark'><h3>Book this tour</h3><p>Free quote within 24 hours — no payment to ask.</p></div><ul><li><span>Duration</span><b>6 days / 5 nights</b></li><li><span>Start</span><b>Tangier</b></li><li><span>End</span><b>Marrakech</b></li><li><span>Style</span><b>North & desert</b></li><li><span>Type</span><b>Private tour</b></li></ul><div class='et-book-f'><a class='et-btn et-btn-wa' href='https://wa.me/212661292596?text=Hello%20Epic%20Travel%20Morocco,%20I%20am%20interested%20in%20the%20Highlights%20of%20Morocco%20(6%20days).%20' target='_blank' rel='noopener'><svg aria-hidden='true'><use href='#et-i-wa'/></svg>Book on WhatsApp</a><a class='et-btn et-btn-o' href='mailto:epictravelmorocco@gmail.com?subject=Highlights%20of%20Morocco'><svg aria-hidden='true'><use href='#et-i-mail'/></svg>Email us</a><a class='et-btn' href='https://epictravelmorocco.com/contact-2/'>Send a request</a><small>WhatsApp +212 661 292 596 · Tel +1 579 484 7707</small></div></div></aside></div></section><section class='et et-sec et-pat'><div class='et-wrap'><div class='et-head'><div class='et-orn'><svg aria-hidden='true'><use href='#et-i-star'/></svg></div><span class='et-eye'>You may also like</span><h2>More Morocco tours</h2></div><div class='et-grid'><a class='et-card et-rv' href='https://epictravelmorocco.com/all-tour/morocco-north-to-south-explorer/'><div class='et-card-img'><img src='https://epictravelmorocco.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/GettyImages-122137131-592426555f9b58f4c07ffd43-600x810.jpg' width='600' height='810' alt='Morocco North to South Explorer – Morocco tour' loading='lazy' decoding='async' data-o='https://epictravelmorocco.com/wp-content/u